    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm seeing some issues where the temperature in the calipers is spiking unexpectedly during the transitions between braking phases. It's almost like the heat is behaving inconsistently, as if something is disrupting the steady state of the thermal dissipation. How do these material differences affect the risk of sudden, unpredictable heat soak in the braking system?",
